A body missing a required field, and a later field whose implicit copy the
target does not accept: the diagnostics come in the order the lens is
walked, the body's first.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		x: string
	}
	count: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		x:     string
		owner: string
	}
	count: int & <10
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		meta: {
			x: v0_0.meta.x
		}
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		x:     string
		owner: string
	}
	count: int & <10
}
-- out/error --
error[E0346]: ForwardLens produces nothing for meta.owner, which v1.0 requires
  --> history/1.0.thema:12:3
   |
12 |         meta: {
   |         ^^^^
   |
   = help: add owner: <mapping> to v1_0.meta

error[E0358]: the ForwardLens of v1.0 would copy v0_0.count into count, which does not accept every value of it
 --> history/1.0.thema:9:1
  |
9 | ForwardLens: {
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = note: both v0.0 and v1.0 declare count, so a lens that does not map it copies it
  = note: count in v1.0 is now int & <10, which does not accept every value of the prior int
  = help: map count in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant
